{%- set card = 'gbm' -%}
{%- set title = 'gbm, the global gradient boosted backend' -%}
{% set intended %}
The gbm backend forecasts hourly demand for every balancing authority in the backtest with one
model, 1 to {{ v('policy.horizons') }} hours after a daily origin at {{ v('policy.issue_hour_utc') }}:00
UTC, with quantiles at {{ v('policy.quantile_levels') }}. It is one of the two candidates the
registry judges. It is meant for the demonstration of a day ahead process on EIA-930 data. It is
not meant for grid operations, for authorities outside the backtest, for horizons past two days, or
for a live desk that has a weather forecast rather than the weather that happened.
{% endset %}
{% set data %}
The same panel as own: EIA-930 hourly demand for the {{ v('data.eia.backtest_authorities') }} backtest
authorities with Open-Meteo observed weather, training from {{ v('data.windows.training_start') }},
validation from {{ v('data.windows.validation_start') }}, test {{ v('data.windows.test_start') }} to
{{ v('data.windows.test_end') }}, with the authority and its region as categorical features.
{% endset %}
{% set fit %}
One XGBoost booster with the quantile objective at the five served levels, on the same ratio target
and point in time features as own plus the authority and region codes, trained on every
{{ v('backtest.gbm.origin_day_thinning') }} origin days of the previous {{ v('policy.gbm_training_window_days') }}
days and refit at the start of every calendar month of the test year ({{ v('backtest.gbm.refits') }}
refits: {{ v('backtest.gbm.refit_dates') }}; {{ v('backtest.gbm.training_rows_calibration') }} rows in the
calibration fit). Intervals conformalized per {{ v('policy.conformal_horizon_bucket_hours') }} hour
bucket on the validation year ({{ v('backtest.gbm.calibration_rows') }} calibration rows). The
backtest took {{ v('backtest.gbm.run_seconds') }} seconds over {{ v('backtest.gbm.origins') }} origins.
LightGBM was the brief's choice and the first implementation; its quantile objective refit too
slowly for the day and XGBoost's vector quantile objective replaced it (`DECISIONS.md`). Version
`{{ v('registry.gbm.version') }}`.
{% endset %}
