{% set contract %}
- [x] **trained**: a calibration fit before the validation year and {{ v('backtest.gbm.refits') }} monthly refits through the test year.
- [x] **timed**: {{ v('backtest.gbm.run_seconds') }} seconds for the backtest, {{ v('backtest.gbm.origins_per_minute') }} origins a minute on CPU.
- [x] **calibrated**: conformalized intervals on the validation year; 90 percent coverage {{ v('backtest.gbm.validation_coverage_90') }} on validation and {{ v('backtest.gbm.coverage_90') }} on test.
- [x] **useful**: MAPE {{ v('backtest.gbm.mape') }} against the seasonal naive's {{ v('backtest.gbm.mape_naive') }}; wins against the operator in {{ v('skill.gbm.h1_24.wins') }} authorities.
- [ ] **fair**: not applicable in the sense of protected groups; the comparability rule keeps the operator comparison honest per authority.
- [x] **gated**: {{ v('registry.gbm.gates_passed') }} of {{ v('registry.gates') }} gates passed ({{ v('registry.gbm.passed') }}).
- [x] **served**: the export `results/models/gbm_model.json` with its booster is what the API loads when the registry names gbm; the registry's choice is {{ v('registry.served') }}.
- [x] **integrated**: the same `POST /v1/forecasts` route serves whichever export the registry names.
- [x] **monitored**: the forecast log and scorecard as for own.
- [x] **documented**: this card, `docs/protocol.md`.
- [x] **bounded**: the intended use above; every {{ v('backtest.gbm.origin_day_thinning') }} origin days in training, stated.
- [x] **validated**: the cross check against own on the same rows ({{ v('skill.crosscheck.disagreements') }} disagreements on the operator) and the leakage check shared with own.
- [x] **explainable at the decision**: the feature importance table above and the per row quantiles stored with every issued forecast.
{% endset %}
{% set limitations %}
Observed weather, as for own. A global model pools authorities that behave differently; the
authority code is a categorical feature, not a separate model. Training on every
{{ v('backtest.gbm.origin_day_thinning') }} origin days was a compute decision for the day and is
stated. The monthly refit is a stated schedule, not a data driven one. The booster is the last
refit's, so the API forecasts with a model fit at the start of the last test month.
{% endset %}
